Additional firmware review
The post-confirmation check now re-queries Block I/O and the target device path
and compares a saved path snapshot, media ID, capacity and required flags.
Firmware tail clearing uses the same bounded33-sector policy with readback.
Review found that the IA32 foreign-call adapter had supplied zero for the high
32 bits of a block address. That is insufficient for tail I/O above2TiB.
The adapter now passes a masked low word and the actual high word for both
read and write. A dedicated sparse-large-disk firmware check must be reported with
the firmware verification results; this report does not infer it from small
VM disks or from native-host tests.
